Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["gCorrelation", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{
  3.832287125521948*^9},ExpressionUUID->"4f1d6608-d3e9-4fed-8ac1-\
25675e972bcf"],

Cell["\<\
We will typically start network partition with a matpac that has been \
subsetted using GeneSubset or CellSubset or both.  Even though the original \
matrix may have been preprocessed to remove rows or columns that are purely \
zeros, such rows or columns may occur in these submatrices.  Thus, before \
doing any correlation we need to remove these with another CutDown step.  \
Then, we we do the correlation, we replace the 1\[CloseCurlyQuote]s on the \
diagonal with zeros, and we lower-triangularize the symmetric matrix, \
throwing away the 50% of values that are redundant.  

 Finally, we re-package the result as a matpac, but now the gene labels apply \
to both the rows and the columns.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.832285371751758*^9, 3.832285373783445*^9}, {
  3.832286198383704*^9, 3.832286225188513*^9}, {3.832286404167581*^9, 
  3.832286465546619*^9}, {3.832287256006316*^9, 3.832287391153638*^9}, {
  3.832287424508676*^9, 3.832287462072431*^9}, {3.833294521827186*^9, 
  3.833294552121502*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"70b9df2b-89f5-4619-b4fe-\
8805c38f9c92"],

Cell["\<\
This version of gCorrelation does two things to compress the result; First it \
sets to zero any values that are below a threshold; next it saves the matrix \
as a Sparse Array
 Finally, we re-package the result as a matpac, with the gene labels applying \
to both the rows and the columns.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.832285371751758*^9, 3.832285373783445*^9}, {
  3.832286198383704*^9, 3.832286225188513*^9}, {3.832286404167581*^9, 
  3.832286465546619*^9}, {3.832287256006316*^9, 3.832287391153638*^9}, {
  3.832287424508676*^9, 3.832287462072431*^9}, {3.833294521827186*^9, 
  3.833294552121502*^9}, {3.834435449821931*^9, 3.8344355043996468`*^9}, {
  3.8345840858568363`*^9, 
  3.834584141713768*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"69ee8574-4ca5-4b88-ace3-\
6367650702e9"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"Options", "[", "gCorrelation", "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"\"\<Min Corr Pos\>\"", "\[Rule]", "0.15"}], " ", ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"\"\<Min Corr Neg\>\"", "\[Rule]", " ", "0.05"}]}], "}"}]}], 
  ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"gCorrelation", "[", 
   RowBox[{"matpac_", ",", " ", 
    RowBox[{"OptionsPattern", "[", "]"}]}], "]"}], ":=", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", " ", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"CutDown", "[", 
       RowBox[{"matpac", ",", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<ValueThresh\>\"", "\[Rule]", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<CellNumber\>\"", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"With", "[", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{"m2", "=", 
        RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{"LowerTriangularize", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"Correlation", "[", 
            RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
             RowBox[{"m", "[", 
              RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"-", "1"}]}], "]"}], "]"}]}], " ", "}"}], ",", 
      "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
      RowBox[{"{", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"SparseArray", "[", 
         RowBox[{"m2", "*", 
          RowBox[{"BoolEval", "[", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"m2", ">", 
             RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<Min Corr Pos\>\"", "]"}]}], " ",
             "||", " ", 
            RowBox[{"m2", "<", 
             RowBox[{"-", 
              RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<Min Corr Neg\>\"", "]"}]}]}]}],
            "]"}]}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"m", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
        RowBox[{"m", "[", 
         RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Metadata\>\"", "\[Rule]", " ", 
         RowBox[{"Join", "[", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"\"\<Metadata\>\"", "/.", 
            RowBox[{"Last", "[", "matpac", "]"}]}], ",", 
           RowBox[{"{", 
            RowBox[{"\"\<Minimum_PCCs\>\"", " ", "\[Rule]", "  ", 
             RowBox[{"{", 
              RowBox[{
               RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<Min Corr Neg\>\"", "]"}], ",",
                " ", 
               RowBox[{"OptionValue", "[", "\"\<Min Corr Pos\>\"", "]"}]}], 
              "}"}]}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "}"}]}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
     "]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8322862820578213`*^9, 3.832286284843957*^9}, {
   3.832286471000395*^9, 3.832286485584445*^9}, {3.832286676528653*^9, 
   3.832286686917441*^9}, {3.8322867222785683`*^9, 3.832286735685976*^9}, {
   3.832286948441029*^9, 3.832287002050454*^9}, {3.8322870991695757`*^9, 
   3.832287117317519*^9}, {3.832287170196826*^9, 3.8322871882578297`*^9}, 
   3.832287356383194*^9, {3.832287470465826*^9, 3.832287505513667*^9}, {
   3.832287863813539*^9, 3.832287867559842*^9}, {3.8332945559227858`*^9, 
   3.833294562844245*^9}, {3.8344104352615623`*^9, 3.834410558793219*^9}, {
   3.8344106183220997`*^9, 3.834410712007388*^9}, 3.8344113090198307`*^9, 
   3.8344114666804123`*^9, {3.8350163691344833`*^9, 3.835016445508675*^9}, {
   3.835016572323846*^9, 3.835016573374115*^9}, {3.846444876069409*^9, 
   3.8464449527040453`*^9}, {3.846444999207872*^9, 3.846445008602127*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],
 CellLabel->"In[57]:=",ExpressionUUID->"4b44a02a-094d-4222-b56c-1c4b4635e977"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["sCorrelation", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.832288026719693*^9, 
  3.832288029025141*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"ccbbd1a0-c33e-4309-84f6-\
bc116cea94b0"],

Cell["\<\
For cell-cell correlations, we transpose the matrix within the matpac, and \
reverse the cell and gene name vectors, So now CutDown and work to deliver a \
transposed matrix and labels, which we correlate in the same way as above. \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.832287880988996*^9, 3.8322879396393957`*^9}, {
  3.833297137582271*^9, 
  3.833297148172378*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"3cc7dada-b2b3-4de4-be6a-\
3031a6d2387e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"sCorrelation", "[", "matpac_", "]"}], ":=", " ", 
  "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
  RowBox[{"With", "[", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{"m", " ", "=", " ", 
      RowBox[{"CutDown", "[", 
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"{", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"matpac", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"GetCellNames", "[", "matpac", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"GetGeneNames", "[", "matpac", "]"}], ",", " ", 
          RowBox[{"matpac", "[", 
           RowBox[{"[", "4", "]"}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<ValueThresh\>\"", "\[Rule]", " ", "0"}], ",", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<CellNumber\>\"", "\[Rule]", "0"}]}], "]"}]}], "}"}], ",",
     "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
    RowBox[{"{", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"LowerTriangularize", "[", 
       RowBox[{"ReplacePart", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"Correlation", "[", 
          RowBox[{"Transpose", "[", 
           RowBox[{"m", "[", 
            RowBox[{"[", "1", "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"{", 
           RowBox[{"n_", ",", "n_"}], "}"}], "\[Rule]", " ", "0"}]}], "]"}], 
       "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"m", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", " ", 
      RowBox[{"m", "[", 
       RowBox[{"[", "2", "]"}], "]"}], ",", 
      RowBox[{"\"\<Metadata\>\"", "\[Rule]", 
       RowBox[{"(", " ", 
        RowBox[{"\"\<Metadata\>\"", "/.", 
         RowBox[{"Last", "[", "matpac", "]"}]}], ")"}]}]}], "}"}]}], 
   "]"}]}]], "Input",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.832287514490883*^9, 3.832287528026558*^9}, {
  3.832287655219597*^9, 3.832287839186311*^9}, {3.8332971515800877`*^9, 
  3.833297189414703*^9}, {3.835016467325807*^9, 3.835016504173732*^9}, {
  3.8350167055503483`*^9, 3.835016722084757*^9}, {3.835016873371422*^9, 
  3.8350168758433437`*^9}},
 Background->RGBColor[1, 1, 0],
 CellLabel->"In[59]:=",ExpressionUUID->"eac2b2e6-5a43-4349-9347-5a6d28a1066a"]
}, Closed]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["gNetworkObject", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8322887671291847`*^9, 3.832288771570603*^9}, 
   3.832288804652028*^9},ExpressionUUID->"2b414ea0-035d-479c-82b4-\
a27d39549b38"],

Cell["\<\
This begins with a matpac of expression values, and requires two additional \
parameters, a cutoff, and a minimum number links.  

It begins by calculating the gene X gene Correlation matrix.

Next it proceeds to adjust those correlations so they will produce corrected \
p-values, according to the adjustments outlined in the file \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Fixing Pearson Correlations\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote].  \
There is an option \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Zeros Correction Cutoff\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote], which corrects only in the case of vector pairs \
where the vector with the fewest zeros has no more than this proportion of \
non-zeros.  Its default is set at 0.06, with a minimum of 10, so for larger \
vectors it will test cases with more than 10 non-zero entries, up to 6%; \
however there\[CloseCurlyQuote]s a hard cutoff at 100 cells, just to limit \
the computation time to generate the interpolating function ifunc.  
The function \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ifunc\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] is an \
interpolating function which, given an observed PCC and given the mean \
proportion of zeros in any two vectors that are correlated, will produce an \
alternative pval that should be used to replace the one in the correlation \
matrix.  

Then it identifies only those genes pairs with a correlation that passes some \
test defined by the cutoff, and which have at least a minimum number of links \
to other genes (\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]minlink\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]).  

The default cutoff is an absolute value of a Pearson Correlation Coefficient. \
 The other option is a Benjamini Hochberg FDR.  If FDR is used, the function \
first begins calculating a list of p-values corresponding to the correlation \
coefficients, in order from strongest correlation coefficient to the weakest, \
stopping when it reaches the p-value to no longer meets the Benjamini \
Hochberg FDR criterion.  It then uses that correlation coefficient as the \
cutoff, printing it out as well.  

Making use of  \[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]ArrayRules\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] it \
identifies the positions \
(\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]hits\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]) where there are at \
least the minimum number of links to other genes.  
Using these rows we cut down the matrix into a  network object by deleting \
all rows and columns not present among the hits.  We also do the same to the \
gene names, to produce a list of gene names that match the new rows and \
columns.  

That Sparse Array is then output together with a gene list that corresponds, \
in order, with the rows in the final matrix that the Sparse Array represents. \
 Thus the output of gNetworkObject is a list, the first element of which is \
an n x n sparse Array, and the second is a gene list of length n.    \
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.8322887752505207`*^9, 3.832288890013174*^9}, {
  3.832288932030519*^9, 3.832288974061318*^9}, {3.83228901248962*^9, 
  3.832289027676651*^9}, {3.832289080069088*^9, 3.8322892982518578`*^9}, {
