Cell["\<\
Ideally, we\[CloseCurlyQuote]d like a form of SingleCommunityGraph that shows \
only the positive or only the negative links, eliminating from the graph any \
nodes not so linked, but keeping the nodes in their proper positions so both \
graphs can be compared.  The easiest way to do this is to create a single \
graph, and then have two different ways of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]de-highlighting\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] any nodes that \
are connected only by the \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]wrong\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] kind of link\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.841597138474053*^9, 
  3.841597229077915*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bbab1a43-e4c1-4e78-b30b-\
58326756d70c"]
}, Closed]],

